intercom-interblocks-callout callout-blue"><p>GPT-6 is rolling out in Chat to eligible Pro, Plus, Enterprise, and Business users. If you don’t see <b>GPT-6</b> in the model menu, it may not be available for your account yet.</p><p>GPT‑6 Pro, powered by GPT‑6 Astra, is available in ChatGPT for Pro $100, Pro $200, Business and Enterprise plans. Enterprise access also depends on your workspace’s model-access permissions. Plus plans include GPT‑6 Astra in ChatGPT Work and Codex.</p><p>Astra requires Codex CLI version <b>0.153.0 or newer</b>. If you do not see Astra in Chat, Work, or Codex in the desktop app, open <b>Menu &gt; Check for Updates</b> and install the latest available version. Check manually even if you recently updated through an automatic update notification or the update icon in the sidebar.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>Overview</h1><p><b>GPT-6</b> in Chat lets you choose how much ChatGPT thinks. With Intelligent UI, answers can include text, visuals, and interactive elements. Available models and thinking levels depend on your plan and workspace settings.</p><h2>Other models in ChatGPT</h2><p>GPT-5.6 Sol is designed for complex work across coding, knowledge work and research, cybersecurity, science, computer use, and design. GPT-5.6 Sol Pro is the highest-capability GPT-5.6 option for difficult tasks and longer-running workflows.</p><p>GPT-5.6 Luna is becoming the default model for Free and Go users. <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> Pro remains the Pro option in the GPT-5.6 family. The <b>GPT-6</b> rollout does not retire older selectable models.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>Choose a thinking level</h1><p>In the model menu, <b>GPT-6</b> replaces <b>Latest</b>. Existing <b>Latest</b> selections move to <b>GPT-6</b> at the same effort; explicit <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> selections stay on GPT-5.6. Use the <b>Thinking</b> slider to choose your effort. When <b>GPT-6</b> is selected, <b>GPT-6 Sol</b> powers <b>Instant</b>, <b>Medium</b>, <b>High</b>, and <b>Extra High</b>; <b>Pro</b> uses <!-- -->GPT-6<!-- --> Pro, powered by <b>GPT-6 Astra</b>. Available options depend on your plan and workspace settings.</p><ul><li><p><b>Instant</b> — Fast responses for everyday questions. Free and Go use GPT-5.6 Luna.</p></li><li><p><b>Medium</b> — Standard thinking.</p></li><li><p><b>High</b> — Extended thinking.</p></li><li><p><b>Extra High</b> — The highest thinking level available with GPT-6 Sol.</p></li><li><p><b>Pro</b> — Pro models for difficult tasks and longer-running workflows. Available models include GPT-5.6 Sol Pro and, on eligible plans, GPT-6 Pro.</p></li></ul><p>On Plus and Pro plans, <b>Instant</b> doesn’t automatically switch to a higher thinking level for complex requests. Asking ChatGPT to “think harder” or “think deeply” won’t automatically switch to a different thinking level. ChatGPT can still switch automatically for safety.</p><p>Free and Go users can use <b>Think</b> for harder questions. Think uses GPT-5.6 Luna, not GPT-5.6 Sol.</p><p>Enterprise customers may continue to see the existing model picker until the new controls reach their workspace.</p><p>For automatic switching to <b>Thinking</b> in managed workspaces, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/12003714" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Business models and limits</a> and <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/11165333" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu models and limits</a>.</p><h1>Intelligent UI</h1><p>With GPT-6 in Chat, Intelligent UI can combine text, visuals, and interactive elements when useful. Ordinary text answers are still possible, and no special prompt is required. A response may begin while ChatGPT continues thinking, followed by more detail.</p><p>These capabilities are rolling out on the web and supported updated apps when you use GPT-6 at <b>Instant</b> through <b>Extra High</b>. They are not available with <b>Pro</b> effort, which remains powered by GPT-6 Astra. Availability depends on your plan and workspace access. Update your mobile app to the latest available version. The older ChatGPT desktop apps for macOS and Windows do not support these capabilities; use ChatGPT on the web instead.</p><p>Intelligent UI has no separate usage quota. Existing model, tool, and plan allowances still apply. Changes to a conversation’s appearance don’t change your other chats.</p><h2>Reduce visual elements</h2><p>On ChatGPT on the web, open <b>Settings</b>. Turn off <b>Layout and visuals</b> to reduce visual elements. Some visual elements may still appear; this setting does not switch the entire answer experience to a classic or text-only mode.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>Availability</h1></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Availability by ChatGPT plan</h2><p>The table below shows thinking-level eligibility by plan. <b>GPT-6 Sol</b> powers these levels as <b>GPT-6</b> rolls out to eligible paid users; explicit <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> selections remain on GPT-5.6. Free and Go users receive GPT-5.6 Luna and do not have access to <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b>.</p><div class="intercom-interblocks-table-container"><table><thead><tr><th><span><b>ChatGPT plan</b></span></th><th><span><b>Medium and High</b></span></th><th><span><b>Extra High</b></span></th><th><span><b>Pro</b></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>Plus</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Not included</span></td><td><span>Not included</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>Pro</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>Business</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>Enterprise</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td><td><span>Included</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>Free and Go</span></td><td><span>Not included</span></td><td><span>Not included</span></td><td><span>Not included</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Logged-out users do not have access to GPT-5.6 Sol. Free and Go users do not have access to GPT-5.6 Sol. Their default model is GPT-5.6 Luna, which also powers Think. In Business and Enterprise workspaces, admins may control which models workspace members can use.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-6 Pro availability</h2><p>GPT-6<!-- --> Pro, powered by <b>GPT-6 Astra</b>, is available in ChatGPT for Pro $100, Pro $200, Business and Enterprise plans. Enterprise access also depends on your workspace’s model-access permissions.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-5.6 availability in Work, Codex, and the OpenAI API</h2><p>GPT-5.6 Luna powers the default ChatGPT experience for Free and Go users as it rolls out. Existing availability in Work and Codex is unchanged. Their availability in other products is shown below.</p><div class="intercom-interblocks-table-container"><table><thead><tr><th><span><b>Product</b></span></th><th><span><b>GPT-5.6 availability</b></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span>Work in ChatGPT</span></td><td><span>Sol, Terra, and Luna for Plus, Pro, Business, and Enterprise</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>Codex</span></td><td><span>Terra for Free and Go; Sol, Terra, and Luna for Plus, Pro, Business, and Enterprise</span></td></tr><tr><td><span>OpenAI API</span></td><td><span>Sol, Terra, and Luna</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Terra provides a balance of capability, speed, and cost for everyday work. Luna is the fastest and lowest-cost model in the GPT-5.6 family.</p><p><em>To access GPT‑5.6 in Codex, use one of these minimum versions:</em></p><ul><li><p><em>ChatGPT desktop app (Codex mode): 26.707.30751</em></p></li><li><p><em>Codex CLI: 0.144.0</em></p></li></ul></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-6 Astra in ChatGPT Work and Codex</h2><p>Your Pro plan includes GPT-6 Astra in Chat, ChatGPT Work and Codex.</p><p>Plus plans include GPT-6 Astra in ChatGPT Work and Codex.</p><p>Usage and credit rules in Work and Codex are separate from Chat. For those details, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/20001275" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Work and Codex</a>.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-6.1 Sol in ChatGPT Work and Codex</h2><p>GPT-6.1 Sol is a model option for ChatGPT Work and Codex. It is separate from the GPT-6, GPT-5.6, and GPT-6 Pro options described here for Chat.</p><p>Enterprise and Edu workspace owners must enable model access. For setup instructions, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/11750701" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Managing feature access with role-based access control in ChatGPT</a>.</p><p>For plan availability and usage details, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/20001275" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Work and Codex</a>.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-5.6 regional availability</h2><p>GPT-5.6 does not have a separate country list. ChatGPT access follows the <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/7947663" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT supported countries and territories</a>, and OpenAI API access follows the <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/5347006" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI API supported countries and territories</a>.<br/><br/>Eligible users in supported European locations, including the EEA, Switzerland, and the United Kingdom, and in the UAE can use GPT-5.6 when it is available for their plan and product.<br/><br/>Country availability and inference residency are separate. GPT-5.6 is not currently supported for workloads configured to use UAE inference residency. This does not prevent eligible users located in the UAE from using GPT-5.6 without that residency configuration.<br/><br/>For more information, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/9903489" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data residency and inference residency for ChatGPT</a> and <a href="https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/your-data#data-residency" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">API data residency</a>.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>Usage limits</h1><p>Usage limits depend on your plan, the model and, for managed workspaces, workspace settings. The sections below explain <b>Thinking</b> limits and how <!-- -->GPT-6<!-- --> Pro and <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> Pro allowances work together.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Instant limits</h2><p>Free and Go users have unlimited everyday text chats, subject to abuse-prevention safeguards. Separate limits continue to apply to file uploads, image generation, voice, data analysis, and other tools.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Thinking usage and fallbacks</h2><p>Manually choosing <b>Medium</b>, <b>High</b>, or <b>Extra High</b> uses <b>GPT-6 Sol</b> when <b>GPT-6</b> is selected, or <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> when you explicitly select GPT-5.6. If you reach a <b>Thinking</b> limit, ChatGPT may continue with another available model.</p><p>If you are on a Go plan, select <b>Think</b> for harder questions. Think uses GPT-5.6 Luna, not <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b>.</p><p>ChatGPT displays when an allowance resets when that information is available. You can use another available model or wait until the displayed reset time.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>GPT-6 Pro and GPT-5.6 Sol Pro limits</h2><p>GPT-6 Pro has usage limits. A Pro subscription does not include unlimited use of the GPT-6 Pro model. ChatGPT Work and Codex have separate allowances.</p><p>Pro plans with higher usage allowances include higher limits for Pro models.</p><p>On Pro $200, when you reach your <!-- -->GPT-6<!-- --> Pro weekly limit, ChatGPT automatically switches to GPT-5.6 <b>Thinking</b> at <b>Medium</b>. To use <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> Pro, select <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> in the model menu, then choose Pro. This remains available only while your <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> Pro daily allowance and combined daily allowance have usage remaining.<br/><br/>On Pro $100, both models draw from one weekly allowance. Switching between them does not provide more messages once that shared allowance is exhausted. Business Standard and Premium also share their included allowance across the two models; switching models does not reset or increase that included allowance.<br/><br/>On a Pro plan, reaching a Pro-model limit does not change your subscription. You can use another available model or wait for the relevant allowance to reset. ChatGPT displays the reset time when that information is available.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Managed workspaces and the ChatGPT Pro plan</h2><p>For current managed-workspace limits and credit rates, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/12003714" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Business - Models and Limits</a>, <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/11165333" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Enterprise and Edu models and limits</a>, and the <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/11481834" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Rate Card</a>.<br/><br/>On the ChatGPT Pro plan, some models have separate usage allowances. When you reach a model&#x27;s allowance, that model may be temporarily unavailable until the allowance resets. Reaching an allowance does not by itself mean that your account was restricted.<br/><br/>For more information, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/9793128" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About ChatGPT Pro tiers</a>.<br/><br/>Usage must follow the <a href="https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms of Use</a>. OpenAI uses safeguards to help prevent misuse, which may occasionally result in a temporary usage restriction. ChatGPT notifies you if this happens.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>GPT-5.6 safeguards</h1><p>GPT-5.6 includes protections trained into the model, along with real-time checks and monitoring. Some higher-risk biological and cybersecurity requests may be refused or require additional checks. These safeguards can occasionally affect legitimate requests.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h1>FAQ</h1></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Where is the Higher intelligence setting?</h2><p>On Plus and Pro plans, the <b>Higher intelligence</b> setting isn’t available on ChatGPT web. Use the model picker to choose how much ChatGPT thinks.<br/><br/>In ChatGPT Business, you can find <b>Higher intelligence</b> under <b>Settings &gt; General</b>. This setting controls whether ChatGPT automatically uses additional thinking while <b>Instant</b> is selected.<br/><br/>For more information about automatic thinking in Business, see: <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/12003714" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Business models and limits</a>.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Why don’t I see GPT-6?</h2><p>GPT-6 is rolling out to eligible paid accounts. Look for <b>GPT-6</b> in the model menu; it is not labeled Sol. If it is missing, it may not be available for your account yet. In a managed workspace, your model-access permissions also apply.</p><h2>Why do I not see GPT-5.6 Sol?</h2><p><b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> remains a separate option in the model menu. Selecting it keeps your conversation on GPT-5.6 and its available thinking levels.</p><p>Confirm that GPT-5.6 Sol is included with your plan and that you are signed in to the correct account. If you use a managed workspace, ask an admin whether the model is available for your workspace or role.<br/><br/>Free and Go plans do not include GPT-5.6 Sol. These plans receive GPT-5.6 Luna.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>What happens to my existing model selection?</h2><p><b>GPT-6</b> is rolling out as the current default in Chat for eligible Pro, Plus, Enterprise, and Business users. Existing <b>Latest</b> selections move to <b>GPT-6</b> at the same effort. Explicit <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> selections stay on GPT-5.6, and older selectable models are not being retired by this rollout. Free and Go users receive GPT-5.6 Luna.<br/><br/><br/><b>GPT-6 Sol</b> powers <b>Instant</b> through <b>Extra High</b> where available. Pro effort remains <!-- -->GPT-6<!-- --> Pro, powered by <b>GPT-6 Astra</b>; <b>GPT-5.6 Sol</b> Pro remains available within the GPT-5.6 family.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Can I select GPT-5.6 Terra or GPT-5.6 Luna in ChatGPT?</h2><p>Terra and Luna are not selectable in standard ChatGPT conversations. Depending on your plan, they are available in Work and Codex. Developers can also use them through the OpenAI API.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Does GPT-5.6 change my ChatGPT usage limits?</h2><p>Free and Go users have unlimited everyday text chats. File uploads, image generation, voice, data analysis, and other tools remain subject to separate limits.</p><p><b>Thinking</b> limits depend on your plan. For managed workspaces, see the plan-specific Models and Limits article or the <a href="https://help.openai.com/articles/11481834" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Rate Card</a> for current limits and credit rates. GPT-6 Pro and GPT-5.6 Sol Pro have the separate or shared Pro-model allowances described above.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Can Support reset my usage limits?</h2><p>No. OpenAI Support does not reset ChatGPT or Codex usage limits. If you reach a limit, wait until it resets or use another available option shown in your account.<br/><br/>If you believe your usage was counted incorrectly, or access has not returned after the stated reset time, contact Support so we can investigate.</p></div><div class="intercom-interblocks-callout callout-transparent"><h2>Don’t see Astra in the desktop app?</h2><p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <b>Menu &gt; Check for Updates</b> and install the latest available version. Check manually even if you recently updated through an automatic update notification or the update icon in the sidebar.</p><p>Astra availability in Chat, Work, and Codex depends on your plan and workspace permissions.</p><p>For the Codex CLI, Astra requires <b>version 0.153.0 or later</b>.</p></div></div></article><section class=""><h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800">Was this article helpful?</h2><form class="flex flex-col gap-4" data-discover="true" action="/resources/feedback" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="article_id" value="20001354"/><div class="flex items-center gap-4"><button type="button" class="rounded-md p-2 transition-colors text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-600" aria-label="Thumbs up" data-btn-label="Thumbs up"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12.1318 2.50389C12.3321 2.15338 12.7235 1.95768 13.1241 2.00775L13.5779 2.06447C16.045 2.37286 17.636 4.83353 16.9048 7.20993L16.3519 9.00709C16.6909 9.01325 16.9965 9.02475 17.2705 9.04623C17.8749 9.09359 18.4313 9.19498 18.9358 9.46056C19.976 10.0082 20.7227 10.9858 20.9774 12.1335C21.1009 12.6901 21.0523 13.2536 20.9389 13.8491C20.8283 14.4307 20.6346 15.1409 20.397 16.0119L19.9295 17.7261C19.9127 17.7876 19.8962 17.8484 19.8799 17.9083C19.5842 18.996 19.3618 19.8139 18.8745 20.4449C18.4468